Title: Jim Titus
Order: 19
Production Code: 1x19

INT. TELASSAR - UNDERGROUND CHAMBER - NIGHT

AMB: distant, muffled

A scream jolts [[Reuel Briggs]] awake. He follows a shadow he knows to be [[Mira]] through unfamiliar corridors, to a wall that opens onto [[Ai]]'s startled face.

AI
Back, Ergamenes! How come you here?

REUEL BRIGGS
I was led. Tell me.

Inside: [[Charlie Vance]], unconscious but alive, and [[Jim Titus]], crushed and dying from the serpent trap.

JIM TITUS
(weak)
Are you there, Mr. Reuel?

REUEL BRIGGS
It's me, Jim. How came you to this?

JIM TITUS
I would not be here if I hadn't agreed to take your life. Aubrey Livingston was my foster brother. I could deny him nothing.

REUEL BRIGGS
(reeling)
Aubrey — the instigator, all along?

JIM TITUS
Return home. Rescue your wife — your wife, and yet not your wife. A man may not marry his own sister. Dianthe Lusk is your sister, Mr. Reuel. Aubrey's too. He is your half-brother.

Reuel falls to his knees.

REUEL BRIGGS
(broken)
You know, then — I am Mira's son.

JIM TITUS
I do. He bribed me to put you out of the way by accident. He killed Miss Molly to clear his road to Dianthe. Go home. Watch him — he'll outwit you yet if you don't.

One last breath, and Jim Titus is gone.

AI
(quiet)
Peace, Ergamenes. He belongs to the ages now.

INT. STEAMSHIP - DECK - DAY (ONE MONTH LATER)

AMB: open ocean, engine thrum

[[Reuel Briggs]] and [[Charlie Vance]] sail west for America, [[Ai]] and [[Ababdis]] traveling with them in the guise of servants — Ai standing surety with Telassar's Council for his king's safe return.
